Information about this program can be found on the distribution site:

	http://c2.com/morse

This version is by:

	Jim Wilson and others

Based on original work by:

	Ward Cunningham

---

This is a fork (https://github.com/selimgez/morse) with further
modifications: mastered letters are permanently retired from the lesson
(instead of lingering forever at a vanishing-but-nonzero chance of being
re-asked), the lesson now recognizes when every letter is learned and
resets itself, a crash on retiring the last visible letter is fixed,
answer speed on an immediately-repeated letter no longer skews the
adaptive response timeout, audio quality and volume control were
improved, and the retirement threshold is grounded in where the progress
bar visually reads empty (tunable at runtime via a command-line
argument). See src/Bugs for the full, dated changelog. Distributed under
the same GNU GPL v2 license as the original (see src/COPYING).
